```sh ntexup``` Declarative Document & Presentation Generator

```sh ntexup``` is an open-source, text-based document and presentation generator designed to make the creation of professional, math-heavy, and reusable teaching materials effortless.

### INSTALL

```sh
nuts install ntexup
```

##) EXAMPLE OF USAGE

```sh
nuts ntexup show  file.ntx
```

###) SYNOPSYS (CMD MODE)

```sh
nuts ntexup <option> file.ntx
```

Commands are :

```sh
nuts ntexup reopen
```
reopen last file/folder

```sh
nuts ntexup build-repo --dump
```
build repository

```sh
nuts ntexup list-templates
```
list available templates

```sh
nuts ntexup generate-doc
```
build documentation

```sh
nuts ntexup generate <path>
```
generate file ntexup file/folder

```--output=<path>```
generated file output file/folder path


```sh
nuts ntexup pdf
```
generate pf


```sh
nuts ntexup dump
```
show dump

```sh
nuts ntexup dump
```
show dump


```sh
nuts ntexup install-editor-syntax [--force|-f] all|gedit|intellij|jedit|kate|notepad++|vim|vscode...
```
install NTexUp format (ntx) syntax highlighting for the given editors.


###) SYNOPSYS (UI MODE)

```sh
nuts ntexup show <option>
```


Options are :

```sh
nuts ntexup new
```
create new project

```sh
nuts ntexup new --show
```
create new project and show it

```sh
nuts ntexup --show-log
```
show log panel


```sh
   nuts ntexup show-doc
```
show documentation

```sh
   nuts ntexup show <path>
```


##) EXAMPLES:

# ntexup: generate pdf
nuts -Zy -w test ntexup show myfolder
